From decb70b7941fd3719dcb3ffd16ce7fdae9d35255 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Olvis=20E=2E=20Gil=20R=C3=ADos?= <olvis@ogtechnologies.eu>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 17:53:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] security: comprehensive backend hardening from recon audit

CRITICAL FIXES
- Remove hardcoded Mailgun API key (key-c8d12b7...) from 10 files;
  centralise in utils/mailgunClient.js (reads from MAILGUN_API_KEY env)
- Move session secret from hardcoded literal to process.env.SESSION_SECRET
- Add secure/httpOnly/sameSite cookie flags to express-session config

HIGH FIXES
- Add global Helmet middleware (X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options,
  HSTS, X-DNS-Prefetch-Control, etc.) applied to all routes
- Add global rate limiter: 300 req / 15 min per IP on all endpoints
- Add auth-specific rate limiter: 20 req / 15 min on all login routes
  (/api/auth, /api/emailauth, /api/emaillogin, /api/metamasklogin,
  /admin/email/auth)
- Tighten CORS allowedHeaders from wildcard '*' to explicit list
  [Content-Type, Authorization, x-auth-token, x-requested-with]
- Remove 82 manual Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * overrides across
  22 route and model files (superseded by global cors() middleware)
- Remove plaintext password logging in routes/auth.js and routes/users.js
- Remove decoded JWT payload logging in middleware/auth.js
- Remove token payload logging in routes/emailLogin.js

DEPENDENCY UPGRADES (npm audit fix)
- dotenv ^8.6.0 -> ^16.x
- jsonwebtoken ^8.5.1 -> ^9.x
- @sendgrid/mail ^7.7.0 -> ^8.x
- Reduced total vulnerabilities: 105 -> 59

REMAINING (require breaking changes / manual review)
- netmask (critical) - transitive via pac-resolver; review proxy config
- protobufjs (critical) - transitive via ipfs-core/nft.storage legacy deps;
  consider removing unused IPFS/NFT storage integrations in a future PR

